course: dictionary
lesson: 2742
title: Disabled: a word about people and things
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Disabled is an adjective with more than one meaning. A disabled person has a physical or mental condition that makes some things harder to do, like walking, seeing or hearing. «People who stare at a disabled child usually just don't understand; a short calm answer is enough.» Here disabled describes the child, and the sentence asks us to stay calm and kind.
explain: Disabled can also describe things made for disabled people, such as «disabled access», «disabled parking» or a «disabled toilet». The word tells you who the thing is for. Try the swap check: a disabled parking space is a space set aside for disabled people.
explain: The verb disable means to turn something off or stop it working. In computing, you can disable a setting, such as location tracking, or disable the alarm. The adjective is about people and places, while the verb is about machines and features.
fact: Disabled people can do many things, sometimes in different ways, with wheelchairs, hearing aids, guide dogs or ramps.
fact: «Disabled» describes a person who has a condition that makes some things harder to do.
fact: «Disabled parking» means a space for disabled people.
fact: «Disable» means to turn off or stop something working, such as an alarm.
fact: In 1990 the US passed the Americans with Disabilities Act, and in 2006 the UN agreed a convention on disabled people's rights.
exercise: «People who stare at a disabled child usually just don't understand.» What does disabled tell us about the child? | The child is always angry | The child has lost their way | *The child has a condition that makes some things harder to do | The child is very tall
exercise: Which phrase means a parking space set aside for disabled people? | parking fine | parking ban | parking tickets | *disabled parking
exercise: What does «disable the alarm» mean? | Set the alarm for later | Make the alarm louder | Test the alarm and wait | *Turn the alarm off or stop it working
test: Which sentence uses disable as a verb? | The disabled toilet is on the ground floor | *The clerk will disable the alarm at six | A disabled parking space is near the door | Disabled people can use the ramp
test: Which of these is a fact from the lesson? | Disabled people cannot do anything | Disable means to start a machine | *In 1990 the US passed the Americans with Disabilities Act | Disabled means very fast
exam: «You might let an older or disabled person, or a parent with a baby, go ahead of you.» Why might you do this? | Because you are in a hurry | *Some people need extra help, and kindness matters | Because disabled people must always go last | It is the rule only in shops
